# Normalize text files to LF in the repository. Line-ending-sensitive files
# (shell scripts, Python entry points, Makefiles) must never be checked out
# with CRLF: bash and GNU make reject \r in shebangs, commands, and recipes.
# Compiled C# is pinned too: .editorconfig sets end_of_line=lf and the build
# enforces it (EnforceCodeStyleInBuild + TreatWarningsAsErrors), so an
# autocrlf checkout would fail the compile with IDE0055 formatting errors.
# Data files the tooling edits or parses by line get the same guarantee:
# scripts/start_dedicated_prefab.sh rewrites serveradmin_apm_seed.xml with
# sed -i, both serverconfig templates go through sbconfig.py's line-based
# insert-if-missing, and the scenario catalogs are JSON read by the
# shell/python lanes. A CRLF checkout changes what those tools match.
* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.cs text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
